You are editing a C++17 repository (the workspace root is a git worktree). Do not run git and do not build. Make exactly the two changes below and nothing else.

BACKGROUND (a UI bug): on the Projects page, pressing `r` on a missing BOM line starts the "BomRestock" input mode (App::beginBomRestock in src/app/bom/AppBomProjectActions.cpp) with the input buffer pre-filled with the shortage quantity, but this mode is not listed in the places that render a prompt, so the user cannot see the number being typed (typing "10" onto the hidden default "5" receives 510). We make the prompt and buffer visible, like the neighbouring StocktakeCount mode.

STEPS
1. In src/app/shell/AppShellRender.cpp, function App::renderSearchBarUi(), the boolean `showsPrompt` is built from a list of `inputMode_ == InputMode::...` terms joined by `||`. Add `inputMode_ == InputMode::BomRestock ||` to that list: put it on the same line as `inputMode_ == InputMode::QuantityAdjust || inputMode_ == InputMode::StocktakeCount ||` by inserting it right after `InputMode::StocktakeCount ||` (so the line reads `... inputMode_ == InputMode::StocktakeCount || inputMode_ == InputMode::BomRestock ||`; if that makes the line longer than about 120 characters, put `inputMode_ == InputMode::BomRestock ||` on its own new line directly below instead). Keep the existing parentheses balanced.
2. In src/app/bom/AppBomActions.cpp, function App::activePrompt(), add this line directly after the line `if (inputMode_ == InputMode::StocktakeCount) return "Physical count: ";`:
  if (inputMode_ == InputMode::BomRestock) return "Received quantity: ";
3. Re-read both edited regions; confirm the parentheses/braces are balanced and that InputMode::BomRestock (declared in src/App.h) is spelled exactly like that. Do not change any other mode or file. Reply with the before/after of the two edits.
